.TH VDR-SUITE-BACKEND-AGENT-ENROLL 8 "August 2026" "VDR-Suite" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
vdr-suite-backend-agent-enroll \- create a controlled VDR-Suite Backend Agent enrollment package
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vdr-suite-backend-agent-enroll
.RI [ --database " PATH" ]
.RI [ --backend " ID" ]
.B --output
.I PATH
.RI [ --ttl-seconds " 300..86400" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a one-time enrollment identity bound by the Control Plane to one
existing Backend and writes the bootstrap package atomically with mode 0600.
The raw enrollment token is never printed, placed in process arguments, or
stored in the SQLite database.  Only its verifier is persisted.
.PP
If the protected output package cannot be finalized, the newly created
enrollment is revoked before the command exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --database " PATH"
Suite SQLite database.  The default is
.IR /var/lib/vdr-suite/vdr-suite.db .
.TP
.BI --backend " ID"
Backend binding.  The default is
.BR default .
.TP
.BI --output " PATH"
Required path for the one-time mode-0600 enrollment package.
.TP
.BI --ttl-seconds " SECONDS"
Validity between 300 and 86400 seconds.  The default is 900.
.SH SECURITY
Run this utility only through an administrator-controlled local path.  Transfer
the package through a protected channel and remove every extra copy after the
Agent consumes it.  Enrollment does not grant VDR write permission.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vdr-suite-backend-agent (8),
.BR vdr-suite-daemon (8)
